811
Part 13. Temporary Shelter Expansion
812 35A-16-1301. Temporary shelter expansion -- Definitions -- Requirements -- Mitigation.
- 25 -

HB0308 compared with HB0308S01
814 (1) As used in this part, "municipal consent" means the written approval from a municipality in which
a congregate shelter is located to the office and to a service provider for temporary expansion of a
congregate shelter's designated bed capacity.
817 (2) A service provider may expand the capacity limit of a congregate shelter up to 135% of the shelter's
designated bed capacity to provide temporary shelter to individuals experiencing homelessness if:
820 (a) the service provider informs the office of the need to temporarily expand the capacity limit of the
shelter;
